@* Data for Plasma-Material Interaction rates.

% $Id$

% $Log$
% Revision 1.1  1996/03/01 20:38:16  dstotler
% Add to repository.
%

\ID{$Id$}

@I pmiformat.hweb
@I problem.hweb

Data for Plasma Material Interactions is held in arrays in common blocks \ldots.
|pd_yield(i,j,k,l,m,p)| accesses the data for the $p$th PMI as an array
with up to 5 dimensions.
Data used in handling the PMI are stored 
in the  |pd_handling| array.

@m pd_yield(i,j,k,l,m,p) pmi_yield_tab[i+pmi_yield_tab_index[1,p]*(j+pmi_yield_tab_index[2,p]*(k+pmi_yield_tab_index[3,p]*(l+pmi_yield_tab_index[4,p]*m)))+pmi_yield_base[p]]

@m pd_yield_indep_var(i,r,p) pmi_yield_indep_var_tab[i+pmi_yield_indep_var_base[r,p]]

@m pd_handling(i,j,k,l,m,d,p) pmi_handling_tab[i+pmi_handling_tab_index[1,d,p]*(j+pmi_handling_tab_index[2,d,p]*(k+pmi_handling_tab_index[3,d,p]*(l+pmi_handling_tab_index[4,d,p]*m)))+pmi_handling_base[d,p]]

@m pd_handling_indep_var(i,r,d,p) pmi_handling_indep_var_tab[i+pmi_handling_indep_var_base[r,d,p]]

@m pd_data_args(x,subs)
      x##_eval_name##subs,x##_rank##subs,x##_var##subs[1],x##_tab_index##subs[1],x##_spacing##subs[0],x##_min##subs[1],x##_delta##subs[1],x##_indep_var_tab[0],x##_indep_var_base##subs[1],x##_tab[0],x##_base##subs

@m pd_dep_var_max pf_dep_var_max-1

